dule in right lower lobe superior segment, which was detected at 32 <bold>(A)</bold>, 16 and 8 mAs/slice (not shown in this figure), but not at 4 mAs/slice <bold>(C)</bold> on the CAD system. Note that volume-rendering image obtained at 32 mAs <bold>(B)</bold> is sharper than that obtained at 4 mAs <bold>(D)</bold>.</p></caption><graphic xlink:href="kjr-9-95-g002"/></fig><table-wrap id="T1" position="float"><label>Table 1</label><caption><p>Doses Delivered at Different Tube Currents</p></caption><graphic xlink:href="kjr-9-95-i001"/></table-wrap><table-wrap id="T2" position="float"><label>Table 2</label><caption><p>Detection Performance of CAD System and Actual Doses Delivered</p></caption><graphic xlink:href="kjr-9-95-i002"/><table-wrap-foot><fn><p>Note.-Numbers in parentheses are nodule numbers per case.</p></fn></table-wrap-foot></table-wrap><table-wrap id="T3" position="float"><label>Table 3</label><caption><p>CAD Detection Rates of Nodules with respect to Nodule Location</p></caption><graphic xlink:href="kjr-9-95-i003"/><table-wrap-foot><fn><p>Note.-Numbers in parentheses are sensitivities as %.</p></fn></table-wrap-foot></table-wrap><table-wrap id="T4" position="float"><label>Table 4</label><caption><p>CAD Detection Rates of Nodules versus Patient BMIs</p></caption><graphic xlink:href="kjr-9-95-i004"/><table-wrap-foot><fn><p>Note.-CAD = computer-aided diagnosis, BMI = body mass index, Numbers in parentheses are sensitivities as %.</p></fn></table-wrap-foot></table-wrap></floats-group></article>